title: A component's menu
intro: Right-click a component in the Inspector to reset it, copy and paste its values, or move it. With several entities selected, components only some of them have show greyed, with Add to All.
project: Empty | Component Menu

# Three gems you can pick up; only the green one glows.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Red Gem
set: Sprite.Tint = #FF004D
set: Transform.Position = -3, 0, 0
add: Pickup
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Blue Gem
set: Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
set: Transform.Position = 0, 1, 0
add: Pickup
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Green Gem
set: Sprite.Tint = #00E436
set: Transform.Position = 3, -1, 0
add: Light
set: Light.Color = #00E436
add: Pickup
look: 0, 0, 5

chapter: The menu on a component | Right-click its header
select: Green Gem
say: The green gem has a light, then a collider and the pickup that collects it.
componentmenu: Light > Move Down
expectcomponents: Green Gem = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Light, Pickup
explain: component:Light | Move Up and Move Down | Right-click a component's header for its menu. Move Down puts the light below its collider, and Move Up brings it back. The Transform always stays first.
set: Light.Radius = 7
componentmenu: Light > Reset to Defaults
expectvalue: Green Gem.Light.Radius = 4
expectvalue: Green Gem.Light.Color = #FFD89A
explain: component:Light | Reset to Defaults | Reset to Defaults puts every value back to what a new light starts with: its radius, and its warm color too.
say: Each of these is one step to undo.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Green Gem.Light.Radius = 7
expectvalue: Green Gem.Light.Color = #00E436

chapter: Copy and paste values | From one component to another of its kind
set: Pickup.Amount = 5
componentmenu: Pickup > Copy Values
select: Red Gem
componentmenu: Pickup > Paste Pickup Values
expectvalue: Red Gem.Pickup.Amount = 5
explain: field:Pickup.Amount | Pasted | Copy Values on the green gem's pickup, then Paste Values on the red one's, and it's worth five points as well. Paste works on several entities at once, too.

chapter: Several at once | What only some of them have
select: Blue Gem
select: Ctrl+Red Gem
select: Ctrl+Green Gem
expectpartial: Light = on 1 of 3
expectpartial: Pickup = none
explain: component:Light | On 1 of 3 | With all three gems selected, the Inspector still lists the light that only the green gem has. It's greyed, and says how many of them have it.
click: addall:Light
expectpartial: Light = none
expectvalue: Red Gem.Light.Radius = 7
expectvalue: Blue Gem.Light.Color = #00E436
explain: scene | Every gem glows | Add to All gives the others a copy of it, with the same color and radius, and whatever it needs.
say: So a whole row of enemies can catch up with the one you tuned, in one step.
